      "nets": ["NET0052", "NET0005"],
      "observed": "On the EthernetAndPower sheet, USB connector J6 pin 3 (D+) is on NET0052 and pin 2 (D-) is on NET0005. On the SkylabModule sheet, SKW92A U11 pin 19 (USB-) is on NET0052 and pin 18 (USB+) is on NET0005, so D+ and D- are crossed.",
      "expected": "USB D+ should connect to the module USB+ pin (U11.18) and USB D- to the module USB- pin (U11.19), preserving D+/D- polarity.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "SkylabModule sheet: '19 USB-', '18 USB+', 'NET0052', 'NET0005'"
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "EthernetAndPower sheet: 'D+' pin 3, 'D-' pin 2, 'NET0052', 'NET0005'"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The USB data pair is polarity-reversed, so the SKW92A USB interface will not enumerate or communicate correctly; the board may still receive 5 V power from USB.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design contains a USB D+/D- polarity swap between the USB connector and the SKW92A module, which would disable USB data communication. No other high-confidence schematic anomaly was identified."
}

